{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Independent booleans like isLoading/hasError/isComplete can all end up true at once — one named state value can only ever be one thing.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Pair the single state value with an explicit transition table so only valid moves between states are even possible, not just the common ones you remembered to check for.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Writing the transition table down forces you to decide what deliberately can't happen from a given state — that's usually where the real bugs were hiding in the boolean version.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
